WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.005
FixtureForge helps prototype teams create small, repeatable CSV test fixtures without copying

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:12.010
real records into a demo. This edited walkthrough uses actual browser captures and synthetic

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:18.015
narration. All orders and category values shown are invented. The app runs locally in the

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:24.020
browser, without sign in, an API key or a data upload.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:31.642
Start with a recipe: forty rows, a fixed seed, and four columns. Order identifiers are

00:00:31.642 --> 00:00:38.263
consecutive integers. Regions come from four choices. Item counts range from one to twelve, and

00:00:38.263 --> 00:00:44.884
amounts range from ten to two hundred at cent precision. Amounts have a ten percent probability

00:00:44.884 --> 00:00:51.505
of being missing. That is a sampled probability, not an exact quota.

00:00:52.505 --> 00:00:58.837
Generate produces forty rows and reports three missing cells for this specific seed. The table

00:00:58.837 --> 00:01:05.168
previews the first ten records, including a missing amount in row eight. The same version, seed

00:01:05.168 --> 00:01:11.499
and complete recipe reproduce the same values. Changing the seed or column order changes the

00:01:11.499 --> 00:01:17.830
generated fixture. This generator is deterministic, not cryptographic randomness.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:25.074
Download CSV exports all forty rows, while recipe JSON keeps the parameters for reproduction.

00:01:25.074 --> 00:01:31.318
Both actual downloads were inspected. CSV quotes commas, newlines and embedded quotes. Common

00:01:31.318 --> 00:01:37.562
spreadsheet formula prefixes in category text receive an apostrophe; negative numeric values

00:01:37.562 --> 00:01:43.806
stay numeric. This is a precaution, not a guarantee for every spreadsheet program. The app does

00:01:43.806 --> 00:01:50.049
not yet import recipe files.

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:56.155
A changed recipe invalidates the previous result immediately. Here editing the region column

00:01:56.155 --> 00:02:01.260
hides both the table and download buttons, and asks us to generate again. That prevents an old

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.365
fixture from being exported as if it reflected the edited settings. No inputs or results are

00:02:06.365 --> 00:02:11.470
saved after a page reload.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:18.961
Generating with a duplicate column name produces a readable error, even when only letter case

00:02:18.961 --> 00:02:25.452
differs. Nine core tests cover repeatability, bounds, decimal precision, missing values,

00:02:25.452 --> 00:02:31.942
validation and CSV edge cases. Codex assisted with code, tests, documentation and this demo.

00:02:31.942 --> 00:02:38.433
FixtureForge does not anonymize data, enforce relationships between columns, or simulate a real

00:02:38.433 --> 00:02:44.924
population. Use invented categories and review exports before sharing.
